{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I've been reviewing why you came in. You've been having abdominal pain, nausea, chest pain, and eye swelling—is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. The belly pain and vomiting have gotten worse over the last two weeks. I think it might be from restarting methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good point. Methotrexate can sometimes cause nausea and stomach upset. We also saw your CT scan—it didn’t show a bowel obstruction or blood clot in your neck, which we were worried about."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. I was scared it was my Crohn’s acting up again or another blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your Crohn’s doesn’t seem to be flaring—no diarrhea or bleeding. But your abdomen is tender, and you hadn’t passed gas in 24 hours when you arrived, so we’re watching closely for pseudo-obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pseudo-obstruction? What’s that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s when the bowel acts blocked, but there’s no physical obstruction. It can happen after surgeries or with certain medications. We’ll keep you NPO for now and give IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the chest pain? It wakes me up at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ECG was normal, and your troponins are negative, so it’s unlikely to be your heart. It might be from straining when you vomit or gas buildup. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eyes were swollen. That’s gone now, but I had a weird noise in my ear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The eye swelling resolved, which is reassuring. The ear thing and the lung changes on your CT are a bit unclear. But your ANCA test was negative, so it’s probably not vasculitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lung changes? What kind of changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There are some small nodules and hazy spots in your lungs. They’ve been there before, and a pulmonologist reviewed them—they don’t look like infection or cancer. We’ll follow with X-rays."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief. Can I at least get my Dilaudid on schedule? I need it every few hours for the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-11-01 02:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve started your usual IV Dilaudid, Benadryl, and diazepam as needed. We’ll keep it consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your belly is more distended today, and you’re still nauseated. We’re going to place an NG tube to help decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "An NG tube? I hate those. It’s so uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know it’s not pleasant, but it will help reduce the pressure and nausea. We’ll make sure it’s placed correctly with an X-ray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, if it helps. How much fluid came out?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Over 2.5 liters already. That’s a lot, and it confirms your bowel isn’t moving things through properly. But no obstruction on imaging—this supports pseudo-obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a real blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-11-02 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not a physical one. Your bowel just isn’t contracting well. We’ll keep the NG tube in for a few days and let your gut rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-11-03 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat X-rays show no change—still no obstruction. The NG tube is working. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-11-03 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, but the pain is a bit better. Can I try sipping water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-11-03 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We need to make sure your bowel is ready. We’ll wait until your nausea improves and the NG output decreases."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-11-04 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back negative, so we’re stopping the Cipro. The initial test showed bacteria, but it wasn’t a true infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-11-04 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried about a UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-11-04 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No need. Your symptoms are from your gut, not your bladder. We’re also stopping methotrexate for now—it might be contributing to your nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-11-04 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I restart it later?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-11-04 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discuss it with your GI doctor. Given your reaction, they might adjust the dose or switch meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-11-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your NG output has decreased, and you’re less bloated. We’re going to try removing the tube and start clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-11-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank goodness. I pulled it out once yesterday, but then I vomited and they put it back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-11-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. This time, we’ll go slow—sips of water, then broth. If you keep it down, we’ll advance your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-11-06 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the clear liquids well. Today, we’ll try soft solids—applesauce, toast, maybe some Ensure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-11-06 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hungry. Can I have more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-11-06 07:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s not rush. Your gut has been through a lot. We’ll build up slowly to avoid setbacks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-11-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you passed gas and had a small bowel movement. That means your gut is waking up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-11-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally! I was starting to worry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-11-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Me too. We’ll keep advancing your diet. You’re on track to go home soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-11-08 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been tolerating soft foods well. No vomiting, pain is controlled with oral meds. We’re thinking discharge in a couple of days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-11-08 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my lung nodules? Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-11-08 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pulmonologist says they’re stable and likely not serious. No signs of infection or cancer. Just follow up with chest X-rays as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-11-08 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eye swelling and ear noise?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-11-08 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The eye swelling resolved on its own. The ear thing doesn’t seem linked to anything serious. If it persists, see ENT as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-11-09 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’re on your regular pain meds by mouth, eating soft foods, and your abdomen is soft. We’re planning discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-11-09 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What meds will I go home on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-11-09 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before—Dilaudid, tramadol, oxazepam, Pepogest, Slomag. We’re restarting bupropion too, since you stopped it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-11-09 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And methotrexate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-11-09 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hold off for now. Talk to your GI doctor before restarting. We’ll send a note to them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-11-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge tomorrow. You’re stable, pain is controlled, and you’re tolerating food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-11-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-11-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop severe pain, can’t keep food down, run a fever, or stop passing gas, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-11-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-11-10 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your PCP in a week, GI doctor to discuss methotrexate, and pulmonology for chest X-rays. We’ll send all the records."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-11-11 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-11-11 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel much better. Still a little tired, but the pain is way down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-11-11 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your body’s been through a lot. Keep resting, eat small meals, and take your meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-11-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Here’s your discharge summary and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-11-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad this is over."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-11-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if anything changes. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-11-01 02:10:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-11-12 15:31:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a history of Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, SVC syndrome, and multiple prior surgeries was admitted for worsening abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, headache, and bilateral eye swelling. Initial imaging ruled out small bowel obstruction, pulmonary embolism, and recurrent SVC syndrome. Abdominal symptoms were attributed to pseudo-obstruction, likely exacerbated by recent re-initiation of methotrexate. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, IV fluids, and an NG tube that drained over 2.5 liters. The NG tube was eventually removed as she improved. Methotrexate was discontinued due to suspected contribution to symptoms. Chest pain was deemed non-cardiac, and lung nodules with ground-glass opacities were determined to be stable and chronic after pulmonology review. Eye swelling resolved spontaneously. She advanced to a soft diet, passed gas, and had a bowel movement prior to discharge. She was discharged home in stable condition on her baseline medications with follow-up arranged with PCP, GI, and pulmonology.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Opioid type dependence, continuous",
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Enlargement of lymph nodes",
      "Other diseases of lung, not elsewhere classified",
      "Headache",
      "Edema of eyelid",
      "Other constipation",
      "Myalgia and myositis, unspecified",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Other chest pain"
    ]
  }
}
